We also know that  $a<b+c$ ,  $b<a+c$ , dan  $c<a+b$ Therefore, the only combination of (a,b,c) are (2,2,3) and (1,3,3). We can find the area of each of them.

For (2,2,3),
\begin{align*}
    \sqrt{\frac{7}{2}(\frac{7}{2}-2)(\frac{7}{2}-2)(\frac{7}{2}-3)} = {\frac{\sqrt{63}}{4}}
\end{align*}

For (1,3,3),
\begin{align*}
    \sqrt{\frac{7}{2}(\frac{7}{2}-1)(\frac{7}{2}-3)(\frac{7}{2}-3)} = {\frac{\sqrt{35}}{4}}
\end{align*}

