    &= a + bi + \frac{a-bi}{a^2 + b^2} 
    &= (a + \frac{a}{a^2+b^2}) + (b-\frac{b}{a^2 + b^2})i 
    &= \frac{10}{9}a + \frac{8}{9}bi
\end{align*}

Since  $|w| = 3$  traces out a circle on the complex plane, it follows that each point on  $\frac{10}{9}a + \frac{8}{9}bi$  satisfies  $\text{Re}(z) = \frac{10}{9}\text{Re}(w)$  and  $\text{Im}(z) = \frac{8}{9}\text{Im}(w)$ . The curve of  $z$  traces out an ellipse on the complex plane with major axis  $\frac{10}{9} \cdot 6$  and minor axis  $\frac{8}{9} \cdot 6$ , which has an area of  $\boxed{\frac{80}{9}\pi}$ .

