Let the roots of  $P(x)$  be  $\tan(A)$ ,  $\tan(B)$ , and  $\tan(C)$ . Then, by Vieta's,
\begin{align*}
\tan(A) + \tan(B) + \tan(C) &= -\sqrt{6} 
\tan(A)\tan(B) + \tan(B)\tan(C) + \tan(C) + \tan(A) &= -\sqrt{2} 
\tan(A)\tan(B)\tan(C) &= \sqrt{3}
\end{align*}
Then, through tangent addition, we have:
\begin{align*}
\tan\left(A+B+C\right) = \dfrac{\tan\left(A\right) + \tan\left(B\right) + \tan\left(C\right) - \tan\left(A\right)\tan\left(B\right)\tan\left(C\right)}{1 - \left(\tan\left(A\right)\tan\left(B\right) + \tan\left(B\right)\tan\left(C\right) + \tan\left(C\right)\tan\left(A\right)\right)} = -\sqrt{3}.
\end{align*}
