\[\frac{2i}{p}\binom{p}{2i}=\frac{(p-1)(p-2)\dots(p-(2i-1))}{(2i-1)!}\equiv \frac{(-1)(-2)\dots(-(2i-1))}{(2i-1)!}\equiv -1\pmod{p}.\]
Hence,
\begin{align*}
    \sum_{i=1}^{(p-1)/2}i^{p-2} &\equiv -\sum_{i=1}^{(p-1)/2} i^{p-2}\frac{2i}{p}\binom{p}{2i}\equiv -\frac{2}{p}\sum_{i=1}^{(p-1)/2} i^{p-1} \binom{p}{2i}
    &\equiv -\frac{2}{p}\sum_{i=1}^{(p-1)/2} \binom{p}{2i}\pmod{p}
\end{align*}
The last summation counts the even-sized nonempty subsets of a  $p$ -element set, of which there are  $2^{p-1}-1$ .

