	&= \frac{2(x^3y+y^3z+z^3x)+4xyz(x+y+z) + \sum_{\text{cyc}} \left( x^3y + 2x^{\frac{3}{2}}yz^{\frac{3}{2}} - 3x^2yz \right)}{x^3y+y^3z+z^3x+2xyz(x+y+z)}  
	&\ge \frac{2(x^3y+y^3z+z^3x)+4xyz(x+y+z)}{x^3y+y^3z+z^3x+2xyz(x+y+z)}  
	&= 2.
	\end{align*}
Here, we have applied Vasc's Inequality followed by AM-GM as  $x^3y + 2x^{\frac{3}{2}}yz^{\frac{3}{2}} \ge 3x^2yz$ .

