Suppose  $(PSR)$  and  $(QSR)$  are seperate circles. Since  $\measuredangle PRS = \measuredangle BPS$ ,  $AB$  is tangent to  $(PSR)$  and similarly  $AC$  is also tangent to  $(QSR)$ . Clearly  $BC$  is the radical axis of the two circles. Now, since  $AP = AQ$ ,   $$ Pow_{(PSR)} A = AP^{2} = AQ^{2} = Pow_{(QSR)} A $$    $\text{ which implies } A \in BC$  which is not true, therefore our supposition is false and the points  $P$ ,  $Q$ ,  $R$  and  $S$  are concyclic.  $\square$

