Let the Fibonacci sequence be denoted by  $F_n$ , where  $F_0=0$ ,  $F_1=1$ , and  $F_{n+2}=F_{n+1}+F_n$  for  $n\ge0$ .
First, we'll show that  $F_n>n^2$  if  $n>12$ ,  $F_{12}=12^2$ , and  $F_n<n^2$  if  $n<12$  (the middle one is omitted, actually). By simple <details><summary>calculations</summary>$F_3=2<9=3^2$  $F_4=3<16=4^2$  $F_5=5<25=5^2$  $F_6=8<36=6^2$  $F_7=13<49=7^2$  $F_8=21<64=8^2$  $F_9=34<81=9^2$  $F_{10}=55<100=10^2$  $F_{11}=89<121=11^2$  $F_{13}=233>169=13^2$  $F_{14}=377>196=14^2$</details>,  $F_n<n^2$  for  $3\le n\le11$  and  $F_{13}>13^2$  and  $F_{14}>14^2$ . Now we can show by induction that  $F_n>n^2$  for  $n\ge13$ , with the base cases  $n=13$  and  $n=14$ . If  $F_n>n^2$  and  $F_{n+1}>(n+1)^2$ , we have:  $$ F_{n+2}=F_n+F_{n+1}>n^2+(n+1)^2=n^2-4n-3+(n+2)^2\ge(n+2)^2. $$  Let  $b_i=a_i^2$  for  $1\le i\le n$ .
First suppose that  $n\le12$ . Setting  $b_i=\sqrt{F_i}$  for  $1\le i\le n$  satisfies the condition that  $\max(a_1,a_2,\ldots,a_n)\le n\cdot\min(a_1,a_2,\ldots,a_n)$ . Recall that if three positive reals  $x\ge y\ge z$  are side lengths of an acute triangle, then  $x^2>y^2+z^2$ . But if some three of  $b_i$  (call them  $b_a\ge b_b\ge b_c$  are the side lengths of an acute triangle we would have  $F_a>F_b+F_c$ . This gives a contradiction as:  $$ F_b+F_c\le F_{a-1}+F_{a-2}=F_a. $$  Now suppose that  $n\ge13$  and that  $\max(a_1,a_2,\ldots,a_n)\le n\cdot\min(a_1,a_2,\ldots,a_n)$ . Also assume FTSOC that no three of  $a_1,a_2,\ldots,a_n$  are side lengths of an acute triangle. WLOG  $b_1\le b_2\le\ldots\le b_n$ , then  $n^2b_1\ge b_n$ , and notice that for all  $x,y,z\in\{1,2,\ldots,n\}$  with  $x>y>z$  we have  $b_x\ge b_y+b_z$ .

We claim that  $b_n\ge F_{k+1}b_{n-k}+F_kb_{n-k-1}$  for all  $0\le k\le n-2$ , which we will show by induction on  $k$ . The base case is just  $b_n\ge b_n$ , which is true. Also, if  $b_n\ge F_{k+1}b_{n-k}+F_kb_{n-k-1}$  for some  $0\le k\le n-1$ , then:
\begin{align*}
b_n&\ge F_{k+1}b_{n-k}+F_kb_{n-k-1}
&\ge F_{k+1}(b_{n-k-1}+b_{n-k-2})+F_kb_{n-k-1}
&=(F_k+F_{k+1})b_{n-k-1}+F_{k+1}b_{n-k-2}
&=F_{k+2}b_{n-k-1}+F_{k+1}b_{n-k-2},
